  "notes": [
    "One frame per fixed 192x256 grid cell. All 40 frame rectangles are explicit and exactly on-grid.",
    "Animation indices are zero-based indices into animations[action].frames, not atlas columns.",
    "Enemy pivot points, hitboxes, attack ranges, and FPS values are starting values to tune during playtesting.",
    "Facing left: mirror the drawn frame, retain the pivot, and mirror projectile spawn offsets and attack hitbox horizontally.",
    "When an enemy dies, stop applying body contact damage. Stormwing has no distinct dead pose; play the project's existing death VFX then despawn.",
    "Cannon frame 4 already visually shows a fired orb; do not also render a second orb inside that frame. Spawn the independent projectile once on animation frame index 1.",
    "Do not let the fire animation loop or re-spawn projectiles when the same animation frame is rendered repeatedly.",
    "Sprite poses are hand-directed generated artwork and may require interpolation, frame reordering, or per-entity position stabilization for seamless movement.",
    "Hitboxes are gameplay suggestions, not verified physics assets.",
    "Sprite sheets and preview are RGBA; transparent pixels outside sprites are non-opaque."
